course: dictionary
lesson: 6316
title: Most: the biggest amount
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Most» is a small word with big jobs. It can be an adjective, a pronoun, an adverb or a noun. Most of the time it means the biggest amount or number. The one with the most has more than all the others.
explain: «Most spiders have eight eyes» means nearly all spiders, more than half. Here most does not mean the biggest number of eyes. It means that almost every spider has eight.
explain: Most also helps make long adjectives into their biggest form. We say «the most beautiful», not «beautifullest». «At most» is different: «at most four apples» means four or fewer, never more.
fact: Most means the biggest amount or number.
fact: «Most of» means more than half: «most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor».
fact: «At most» means no more than a number: «at most four» is four or less.
fact: «Most» makes long adjectives into the biggest form: «the most beautiful».
fact: «Make the most of» means use something well, and «most» can also mean very, as in «a most interesting question».
exercise: «Most spiders have eight eyes, but many see poorly.» What does most mean here? | *Nearly all, more than half | Only one | The smallest number
exercise: A box can hold at most four apples. What does at most mean? | *4 or fewer | Exactly ten | 4 or more
exercise: Which phrase uses most to make an adjective into its biggest form? | the beautiful most | very beautifuller | *the most beautiful
test: «Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes.» What does most mean here? | Only a few | *Nearly all, more than half | None at all
test: Ayesha has 12 stickers, Sam has 9 and Ben has 5. Who has the most? | Ben | Sam | *Ayesha
exam: Which sentence uses most to mean very, in a formal style? | Make the most of your time | *That was a most interesting question | At most ten children may enter | Most of the class came early
